<!--
  =========================================================================
  File        : network_security_config.xml
  Project     : Smart Solar Microgrid Trading System - SE4040 Assignment 1
  Author      : NIMSARA R V P P (IT 23215306)
  Created     : 2026-09-20
  Description : The network rule for release builds. HTTPS only.

  What changed and why
                This file used to name each laptop IP so plain HTTP would
                work during the demo. That put the server address in two
                places, here and in the Java, and changing only one gave:
                    CLEARTEXT communication to ... not permitted

                The address now lives in android/local.properties on its
                own. A resource file cannot read that, so rather than keep
                a second copy of it, the permission was moved to a debug
                only version of this file in src/debug.

  What this means
                Release build : plain HTTP is refused outright. Stricter
                                than the old named list.
                Debug build   : src/debug/res/xml replaces this file and
                                allows plain HTTP. That is the build the
                                demo runs on, because IIS on a laptop has
                                no certificate a phone would trust.

  If a release build ever has to reach a plain HTTP server, name that host
  here in a domain-config. Do not turn cleartext on for everything.
  =========================================================================
-->
<network-security-config>

    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" />

</network-security-config>
